<p>Families travelling with young children also tend to prefer the private transfer for the simple reason that it removes several transitions from the day — no walk through a station concourse, no juggling bags on and off a train, no second taxi queue at the far end. A single vehicle that leaves from your door in Zaragoza and arrives at your door in Barcelona keeps the whole trip contained to one continuous leg, which matters more with children or older relatives in the group than it might for a solo traveller.</p>
