<p>Working travellers also use the drive productively, since a private car offers a quieter, more private space than a train carriage for calls or preparation ahead of a Barcelona meeting, without the risk of a patchy signal in a tunnel or a crowded carriage interrupting a call at the wrong moment. For anyone whose Zaragoza-Barcelona trip is squeezed into a single working day, that extra measure of control over the journey itself, not just the destination, can be worth as much as the time saved by faster rail, and it applies just as well on the return leg once meetings in Barcelona are finished and it's time to head back to Zaragoza.</p>
